### 2026-08-30T18:42:11.075Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Understood — stopping there, no more test-suite launches. Here's the round-3 review based on what I already confirmed.

## Round 3 review: `[REDACTED_SECRET]` (Random-as-Simon, silent-clef omission, adaptive timing, non-interruptive play-along)

This is a big, ambitious rewrite and most of it is solid — I read the diffs and confirmed correctness on the silent-clef logic (properly null-guarded throughout `notation.js`), the non-interruptive queued-input design (`pendingUserNotes`/`flushPendingUserNotes`), and the silence-based mistake-replay scheduler. All 20 of the new/updated tests in `tests/melody.desktop.spec.js` pass.

**But there's a real crash regression, and it's not cosmetic.** `randomMelody()` now returns a **1-note** array instead of the old 10-note fallback (correct, by design — Random is now a growing Simon prefix). The problem: `updateDifficultyUI`'s Random-mode decoration loop (`[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`) still does

```js
for (let i = 0; i < current; i++) {
    const midi = melody[i].midi;   // <- no bounds check against melody.length
```

With the old 10-note default this was always safe. With the new 1-note default, any call where `current` (userIndex, or an explicit `overrideIndex`) isn't tightly bounded by the current (now much shorter) array throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'midi')` — **inside the app's own code**, not just test setup. I confirmed this is exactly what's breaking pre-existing tests that Codex's diff never touched:

- `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO] pivots the window on the override, not state.userIndex` — crashes at `melody.js:799`.
- `playing the full melody preview live-updates the note list as it plays` — same root cause, one level up in the test's own follow-on assertion.
- `Melody mode: the start marker sits right before the note it targets` — marker never renders (likely the same crash short-circuiting the render).
- `Melody mode: a wrong note resets progress back to the scrub position, not always to note 0` — wrong index, consistent with a stale/short array.
- `Melody: the next three notes are tri-coloured in the timeline and on the Tonnetz` — upcoming-ranks array empty.

That's 5 failures, and I only found them because I happened to widen my search past my first keyword filter — my initial `-g "Melody|Compose|Notation|Timeline"` grep missed titles like `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]...` that don't contain those exact words, so **the true count could be higher**; I stopped short of a full unfiltered run per your steer just now, so treat 5 as a floor, not a ceiling.

**Root cause, concretely:** the decoration loop needs to stop at `Math.min(current, melody.length)`, not just `current` — the same fix belongs anywhere else in the Random path that assumes `current <= melody.length` now that the array can legitimately be shorter than a caller's index.

This one's worth flagging back to Codex directly rather than waiting for another round.


